.TH MUEMACS 1 "2026" "μEmacs 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
muEmacs \- small, fast Linux terminal text editor (μEmacs)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muEmacs
\fR[\fB+\fR\fIn\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-g\fR\fIn\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-s\fR\fIpattern\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-r\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-n\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-v\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB-e\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB--help\fR]\ |
\fR[\fB--version\fR]
\fR[\fIFILE\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBμEmacs\fR is a C23 modernization of Linus Torvalds' tiny uEmacs editor for contemporary Linux terminals.
It retains the original philosophy: small codebase (~35,000 lines), instant startup, sane defaults, and classic Emacs-style
key bindings in a pure TUI. This implementation focuses on Linux, UTF\-8 correctness, terminal fidelity,
and robust behavior without bloat.
.PP
Notable features:
.IP \(bu 2
O(1) hash-based keymap with hierarchical prefix keys and buffer-local bindings.
.IP \(bu 2
Built-in terminal emulator with full VT100/xterm emulation (\fBC\-x t\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Optional Vim/Evil mode with full modal editing, operators, motions, and text objects.
.IP \(bu 2
Boyer-Moore-Horspool search with Thompson NFA regex and optional parallel search.
.IP \(bu 2
VSCode-style undo grouping with atomic circular buffer (10,000 operations).
.IP \(bu 2
TOML configuration with XDG Base Directory support.
.IP \(bu 2
Three-layer extension system (UEP): native C extensions, Lua scripts, and AI agent orchestration.
.IP \(bu 2
System clipboard integration via OSC 52, xclip, xsel, or wl-copy.
.IP \(bu 2
Encryption via GPG, age, or openssl.
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are recognized on the command line:
.TP
.B --help
Show a brief usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.BI + n
Start at line \fIn\fR of the first file. If \fIn\fR is omitted (plain \fB+\fR), start at end of file.
.TP
.BI -g n
Go to line \fIn\fR after startup (equivalent to \fB+\fR\fIn\fR).
.TP
.BI -s pattern
Search forward for \fIpattern\fR on startup.
.TP
.B -v
View\-only mode (read\-only buffers).
.TP
.B -e
Explicitly enable editing (cancels a prior \fB-v\fR).
.TP
.B -r
Restricted mode: disallow file writes, shell escapes, and similar operations.
.TP
.B -n
Accept NUL (\\0) characters in input files.
.TP
.BI @ file
Execute startup macro file \fIfile\fR before entering the editor.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
μEmacs uses Emacs\-style bindings by default. Selected bindings:
.SS Essential
.TP
.B C\-x C\-c
Exit μEmacs.
.TP
.B C\-x C\-s
Save file.
.TP
.B C\-x C\-f
Find/open file.
.TP
.B C\-g
Abort current command.
.TP
.B M\-x
Execute named command.
.SS Movement
.TP
.B C\-a / C\-e
Beginning / end of line.
.TP
.B C\-f / C\-b
Forward / backward character.
.TP
.B C\-n / C\-p
Next / previous line.
.TP
.B C\-v / M\-v
Next / previous page.
.TP
.B M\-< / M\->
Beginning / end of file.
.TP
.B M\-g
Go to line.
.SS Editing
.TP
.B C\-d / C\-h
Delete next / previous character.
.TP
.B C\-k
Kill to end of line.
.TP
.B C\-w / M\-w / C\-y
Kill region / copy region / yank.
.TP
.B C\-_ / M\-_
Undo / redo.
.SS Windows & Buffers
.TP
.B C\-x 2 / C\-x 0 / C\-x 1
Split / delete / only window.
.TP
.B C\-x o
Next window.
.TP
.B C\-x b / C\-x k
Select / kill buffer.
.TP
.B C\-x t
Open terminal.
.SS Search
.TP
.B C\-s / C\-r
Incremental search forward / reverse.
.TP
.B M\-r / M\-%
Replace / query replace.
.SS Macros
.TP
.B C\-x ( / C\-x ) / C\-x e
Begin / end / execute macro.
.PP
Use \fBC\-u\fR for numeric arguments. ESC or Alt serves as Meta prefix.
.SH TERMINAL EMULATOR
μEmacs includes a built-in terminal emulator accessible via \fBC\-x t\fR, \fBM\-t\fR, or \fBM\-x terminal-buffer\fR.
.PP
Features:
.IP \(bu 2
Full VT100/xterm CSI sequence emulation with cursor addressing and scroll regions.
.IP \(bu 2
PTY allocation via \fBforkpty()\fR with proper signal handling.
.IP \(bu 2
Configurable window height (default 45% of screen).
.IP \(bu 2
Seamless focus switching with \fBC\-x o\fR.
.SS Terminal Commands
.TP
.B terminal-buffer, terminal-create
Open terminal in split window or create named terminal.
.TP
.B terminal-close
Close terminal window.
.TP
.B terminal-list
List all active terminals.
.TP
.B terminal-switch
Switch between terminals.
.TP
.B terminal-toggle
Toggle terminal visibility.
.TP
.B terminal-send-line, terminal-send-region, terminal-send-buffer
Send text to terminal.
.TP
.B terminal-capture
Capture terminal output to buffer.
.SS Build Integration
.TP
.B build-run
Run build command (reads \fBMakefile\fR or prompts).
.TP
.B build-next-error, build-prev-error
Jump to next/previous error location from build output.
.SS REPL Integration
.TP
.B repl-start
Start a REPL for the current filetype.
.TP
.B repl-eval-line, repl-eval-region, repl-eval-buffer
Send line/region/buffer to REPL.
.SH VIM/EVIL MODE
Enable with \fBevil_mode = true\fR in settings.toml or \fBM\-x evil-mode\fR.
.SS Modes
.TP
.B Normal
Navigation and commands (default). Press \fBESC\fR to return.
.TP
.B Insert
Text entry. Enter with \fBi\fR, \fBa\fR, \fBo\fR, \fBA\fR, \fBI\fR, \fBO\fR.
.TP
.B Visual
Character selection (\fBv\fR), line selection (\fBV\fR), block selection (\fBC\-v\fR).
.TP
.B Replace
Overwrite mode (\fBR\fR).
.SS Motions
.TP
.B h/j/k/l
Left/down/up/right.
.TP
.B w/b/e
Word forward/backward/end.
.TP
.B 0/$/^
Line start/end/first non-blank.
.TP
.B gg/G
Buffer start/end (or line N with count).
.TP
.B f/F/t/T
Find/till character forward/backward.
.TP
.B %
Matching bracket.
.SS Operators
.TP
.B d/c/y
Delete/change/yank. Combine with motions: \fBdw\fR, \fBc$\fR, \fByy\fR.
.TP
.B dd/cc/yy
Operate on whole line.
.TP
.B D/C/Y
Operate to end of line.
.SS Text Objects
.TP
.B iw/aw
Inner/around word.
.TP
.B i"/a", i'/a', i(/a), i{/a}, i[/a]
Inner/around quoted strings, parentheses, braces, brackets.
.SS Other
.TP
.B u / C\-r
Undo / redo.
.TP
.B . (dot)
Repeat last change.
.TP
.B p/P
Put after/before cursor.
.TP
.B m{a-z} / '{a-z} / `{a-z}
Set mark / jump to mark line / jump to mark exact.
.TP
.B / / ? / n / N
Search forward/backward, next/previous match.
.TP
.B * / #
Search word under cursor forward/backward.
.SH ENCRYPTION
μEmacs shells out to system encryption tools for secure file handling.
.SS GPG
.TP
.B encrypt-buffer
Encrypt current buffer with GPG symmetric encryption (AES256). Creates \fI.gpg\fR file.
.TP
.B decrypt-file
Decrypt a \fI.gpg\fR file and open in buffer.
.SS Age
.TP
.B encrypt-buffer-age
Encrypt with age tool.
.TP
.B decrypt-file-age
Decrypt age-encrypted file.
.SS Auto
.TP
.B encrypt-buffer-auto
Auto-detect best available tool (gpg > age > openssl).
.TP
.B show-encryption-tools
Display available encryption tools on the system.
.SH CLIPBOARD
Multiple clipboard providers with automatic detection.
.SS Providers
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOSC 52\fR: Terminal escape sequence (works over SSH/tmux). Supported by kitty, alacritty, foot, iTerm2.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwl-copy/wl-paste\fR: Wayland native.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBxclip/xsel\fR: X11 clipboard tools.
.SS Commands
.TP
.B copy-to-clipboard
Copy region to system clipboard.
.TP
.B yank-clipboard
Paste from system clipboard.
.TP
.B clipboard-provider
Show or set clipboard provider.
.SS Configuration
In \fIsettings.toml\fR:
.nf
[clipboard]
provider = "auto"      # auto, osc52, xclip, xsel, wl-copy, none
sync_kills = false     # Sync kill ring to system clipboard
osc52_enabled = true   # Enable OSC 52 when available
.fi
.SH SOFT WRAP
Visual line wrapping without modifying file content.
.TP
.B soft-wrap
Toggle soft wrap for current buffer.
.TP
.B soft-wrap-column
Set soft wrap column (default 80).
.PP
Configure in \fIsettings.toml\fR:
.nf
[wrap]
soft_wrap = false
soft_wrap_column = 80
.fi
.SH WRITING MODE
Prose editing helpers for comfortable long-form writing.
.TP
.B writing-mode
Enable writing mode: sets fill column (default 80) and enables WRAP mode.
With numeric argument: \fBC\-u 72 M\-x writing-mode\fR sets column to 72.
.TP
.B exit-writing-mode
Restore previous fill column and wrap settings.
.TP
.B set-column-width
Set preferred wrap column.
.SH CONFIGURATION
μEmacs uses TOML configuration with XDG Base Directory support.
.SS File Locations
.TP
.I ~/.config/muemacs/settings.toml
User configuration (highest priority).
.TP
.I /usr/share/muemacs/editor/settings.toml
System defaults.
.SS Key Sections
.nf
[editor]
column_width = 80
wrap = false
evil_mode = false
tab_width = 8

[visual]
ruler = true
ruler_col = 80
highlight_line = true

[terminal]
enabled = true
height_percent = 45

[clipboard]
provider = "auto"

[extensions]
timeout = 5000

[extensions.python]
format = "black -q -"

[extensions.c]
format = "clang-format"
.fi
.SS Commands
.TP
.B open-user-config
Open user settings.toml in editor.
.TP
.B list-settings
Display current settings.
.TP
.B save-settings
Save current settings to user config.
.SH UEP FORMAT
Per-filetype formatting via external tools.
.TP
.B uep-format-buffer
Format current buffer using configured provider.
.PP
Providers are configured per filetype in \fIsettings.toml\fR:
.nf
[extensions.python]
format = "black -q -"

[extensions.rust]
format = "rustfmt"

[extensions.go]
format = "gofmt"
.fi
Buffer contents are piped to stdin; formatted output replaces buffer.
.SH EXTENSION SYSTEM (UEP)
The μEmacs Extension Protocol provides native extensibility via shared libraries.
.SS Native Extensions
Shared libraries (\fB.so\fR) loaded via \fBdlopen()\fR from \fI~/.config/muemacs/extensions/\fR.
Extensions can be written in any language that compiles to shared libraries with C ABI.
.PP
Supported languages (with examples):
.IP \(bu 2
\fBC\fR \- git_workflow, write_edit, rg_search
.IP \(bu 2
\fBZig\fR \- SIMD-accelerated search
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGo\fR \- LSP client
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRust\fR \- ripgrep integration
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCrystal\fR \- AI completion via NEUROXUS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFortran\fR \- Git operations via libgit2
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAda\fR \- Fuzzy finder
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHaskell\fR \- Project management
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPascal\fR \- Multi-cursor editing
.PP
Extensions with garbage-collected runtimes (Crystal, Go, Haskell) are loaded with
\fBRTLD_NODELETE\fR to prevent memory issues on unload.
.SS Commands
.TP
.B extension-load
Load extension by path.
.TP
.B extension-unload
Unload extension by name.
.TP
.B extension-list
List loaded extensions.
.SH AI AGENTS
Built-in AI agent orchestration via \fBposix_spawn()\fR.
.TP
.B agent-spawn
Spawn AI agent (Claude by default). Prompts for task, streams output to \fB*agent-<name>*\fR buffer.
.TP
.B agent-list
Show running agents with status.
.TP
.B agent-kill
Terminate running agent.
.TP
.B agent-output
Switch to agent output buffer.
.PP
Up to 4 agents run concurrently. Output is polled in the main loop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.SS Required
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal type (use \fBxterm\-256color\fR or terminal-specific entry).
.TP
.B LANG, LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE
UTF-8 locale for proper Unicode handling.
.SS Optional
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Set to \fBtruecolor\fR for 24-bit color.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base config directory (default \fI~/.config\fR).
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell for terminal emulator (default \fI/bin/sh\fR).
.SS Exported to Subprocesses
When μEmacs spawns shell commands, it exports:
.TP
.B UE_FILENAME
Current file path.
.TP
.B UE_BUFNAME
Current buffer name.
.TP
.B UE_LINE
Cursor line (1-indexed).
.TP
.B UE_COL
Cursor column (0-indexed).
.TP
.B UE_MODIFIED
"1" if buffer modified, "0" otherwise.
.TP
.B UE_FILETYPE
Detected filetype (c, python, rust, etc.).
.TP
.B UE_TERMINAL
"1" when inside μEmacs terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/muemacs/settings.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/muemacs/extensions/
Native extensions (auto-loaded). Supports C, Zig, Go, Rust, Crystal, Fortran, Ada, Haskell, Pascal.
.TP
.I ~/.config/muemacs/agents/
AI agent definitions.
.TP
.I /usr/share/muemacs/editor/settings.toml
System defaults.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/muEmacs.desktop
Desktop entry.
